# Copy this file to .env and fill in real values. .env is gitignored.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Postgres — Neon (https://neon.com). Any Postgres works; the schema declares
# provider = "postgresql", so moving between hosts is these two lines and nothing
# else. Non-Postgres targets are a much bigger change.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Neon gives you two connection strings for the same database. Use BOTH:
#
#   DATABASE_URL  the POOLED one, hostname contains "-pooler"  -> the app
#   DIRECT_URL    the same host WITHOUT "-pooler"              -> migrations
#
# Why the split: the pooled endpoint is PgBouncer in transaction mode, which is
# right for request traffic but holds no session state — so the DDL and advisory
# lock that `prisma migrate` needs are unreliable through it. prisma.config.ts
# points the CLI at DIRECT_URL; src/server/db/client.ts uses DATABASE_URL.
#
# sslmode=verify-full validates the certificate and hostname. Prefer it over
# Neon's default `require`, which in libpq semantics encrypts without verifying.
#
#   npm run db:migrate  create/apply migrations (works on Neon; the old local
#                       WASM server failed this with P1017)
#   npm run db:seed     insert one sample proposal
#   npm run db:studio   browse the tables
#   npm run db:check    print row counts without Studio
#
# Supabase works the same way: pooled string (port 6543) here, direct (5432) below.
#
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@ep-xxx-pooler.region.aws.neon.tech/neondb?sslmode=verify-full&channel_binding=require"
DIRECT_URL="postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@ep-xxx.region.aws.neon.tech/neondb?sslmode=verify-full&channel_binding=require"

# SHADOW_DATABASE_URL is intentionally absent. `prisma migrate dev` needs a scratch
# database to detect drift, and on managed Postgres it creates and drops one
# itself. Only set this if your provider forbids CREATE DATABASE — pointing it at
# a host that isn't running makes migrations fail.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Claude — server-side only. Never expose this to the browser; never prefix it
# with NEXT_PUBLIC_.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY="sk-ant-..."

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Which engine builds proposals. These three values and nothing else:
#
#   offline  keyword matching against the PbN catalog — no API cost, works with
#            no key at all. Transcript-specific, but it cannot understand
#            negation ("forms are fine already"), so every section needs a read.
#   claude   real extraction. Needs a key WITH CREDIT.
#   auto     claude if a key is set, else offline. Same as leaving this unset.
#
# Any OTHER value resolves to `offline` and raises an error toast — it is not
# treated as `auto`. A typo like "onlien" would otherwise find the key and
# quietly start billing the API.
#
# On `auto` and `claude`, a credit / auth / rate-limit failure falls back to
# offline rather than leaving the rep with a dead end.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PROPOSAL_GENERATION="offline"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Public origin, used by proposalUrlFor() to build the shareable link that gets
# written into proposal_tracking.proposal_url.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ means this is INLINED AT BUILD TIME, not read at runtime. On Vercel
# it must be the real deployed origin (https://your-app.vercel.app), and changing
# it later requires a REDEPLOY — editing the variable alone does nothing. Get it
# wrong and reps copy dead links and send them to dentists.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL="http://localhost:3000"
